  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Research note / independent corroboration and exact recursive interface; no new kappa.** PR1155's pinned note says any read of drifting workspace prevents deferred restoration. Nonzero readers can instead preserve the observed value: for distinct outputs, the exact all-input condition is `H_i(P_(i-1)-I)=0`. With one shared output observed only at batch exit, only the sum of defects must vanish. The note proves both statements and gives explicit compatible and incompatible examples.\n\nA noncommuting eight-coordinate, three-child construction includes pre-read cancellation of arbitrary incoming dirt and both complete additive source calls. In the declared fixed borrowing interface, its full emitted word falls from **210 to 150 two-address ADD instructions** and **5864 to 4504 data-tape word transitions**. The recurrence charges source/coefficient access, both recursive directions, routing, scratch restoration, preparation and dispatch. These are exact online invoices, not a runtime benchmark; extra preparation must be paid before claiming an end-to-end gain. Direct evaluation can be cheaper than either toy wrapper. No supplier, selected frontier, upstream file or review ledger changes.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nThe final submission check found Sagar Thakrar's just-opened **#1199**, pinned\nat `85ac2880ea5bda44f28632b71ffa2b4e35ec6b7d`. Its README was inspected. It\nindependently corrects the same claim, implements a diagonal-sign checkpoint\nplanner and states the general summed-defect identity. **No priority is claimed\nfor the correction or identity.** The distinct contribution here is noncommuting\npermutation coverage with independent output ports, a wrapper whose outputs are\nindependent of incoming scratch dirt, and separately implemented symbolic\nscalar/tape accounting. This neither repeats nor supersedes its cut planner.\n\n- OS-random assignment seed **50**, recursive interfaces; task card: `research/invariant-reader-restoration/CLAIM.md`.\n- Exact base: `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`.\n- Nearest predecessor: #1155 at `9821c6e9388f3fc097e94b72be9fa7b41a849527`; its original note is retained unchanged with SHA256/Git-blob pins.\n- #889 already supplies shared-B dirty fanout/echo cancellation; no new batching priority is claimed. The additional evidence is noncommuting reader compatibility through intervening permutations and its independently checked invoice.\n- #1012/#974 price a different hosted-assembly boundary. #1057/#1164 concern dirty-pool allocation and higher-arity echoes. Exact heads are in `SOURCE-PINS.json`.\n- Read the selected #1094 construction/review; refreshed PRs and discussions before submission. No pinned sprint issue existed, so the claim remained local. This does not adopt an unreviewed frontier.\n\n## Validation\n\nCPython 3.14.7 on macOS arm64; standard library only:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/invariant-reader-restoration/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/invariant-reader-restoration/test_package.py\n```\n\nBoth pass. Evidence includes all **5,832** declared two-coordinate reader instances, all **873** permutations through width six, the full emitted map on **19** arbitrary source/workspace/output coordinates, separate symbolic prefix bounds and invoice reconstruction, explicit mathematical failure witnesses, relocation, deterministic certificate export and **eight** on-disk corruption controls. `CERTIFICATE.json` is recomputed and compared field for field. The general theorem is the written algebraic argument, not an extrapolation from finite tests.\n\nNo selected cold replay, hosted CI result, physical supplier admission, full multiplication formalization or new exponent is claimed. Inherited compiler, hosting, precision/tape and analytic obligations remain.\n\n## Credit\n\nPrepared for **mightyOil (Philipp)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance**, including three scoped Codex subagents. Credit Navinor/Aaron Wang (#1155, with opencode), Ross Richardson/CubeJerry (#889), Sagar Thakrar (#1012 and the concurrent #1199 correction/planner), avirazza (#974), Gareth Davidson (#1057), woklerx (#1164), and the retained repository lineage. New files are Apache-2.0; predecessor bytes and notices are retained. AI review is not independent human or proof-assistant review.\n",
